<title>CANADA: CWB DETAILS TOP 1996/97 WHEAT, BARLEY MARKETS.</title>
<headline>CWB DETAILS TOP 1996/97 WHEAT, BARLEY MARKETS.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board on Thursday detailed how much wheat and barley its top clients bought in crop year 1996/97 (Aug/July).</p>
<p>1996/97*  ('000 tonnes)   1995/96</p>
<p>WHEAT (excluding Durum)</p>
<p>1. Canada  2,384.0	1. China    4,729.0</p>
<p>2. Iran    2,027.0	2. Canada   1,970.0</p>
<p>3. China   1,684.0	3. Japan    1,363.0</p>
<p>4. U.S.A.  1,555.0	4. Brazil   1,110.0</p>
<p>5. Japan   1,444.0	5. Indonesia  889.0</p>
<p>DURUM</p>
<p>1. Algeria 1,218.0	1. Algeria  1,128.0</p>
<p>2. Iran	609.0	2. Belgium    277.0</p>
<p>3. U.S.A.    361.0	3. Italy	269.0</p>
<p>4. Venezuela 296.0	4. Canada     253.0</p>
<p>5. Canada    245.0	5. Morocco    223.0</p>
<p>FEED BARLEY</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia 991.0	Saudi Arabia  370.0</p>
<p>2. Japan     527.0	2. Japan	312.0</p>
<p>3. Iran	158.0	3. U.S.A.	93.0</p>
<p>4. U.S.A.    142.0	4. Mexico	57.0</p>
<p>5. S.Korea    51.0	5. Iran	  53.0</p>
<p>MALTING BARLEY</p>
<p>1. Canada  1,082.0	1. Canada     992.0</p>
<p>2. U.S.A.    755.0	2. U.S.A.     692.0</p>
<p>3. China     516.0	3. China	379.0</p>
<p>4. Japan	48.0	4. Colombia   146.0</p>
<p>5. Argentina  37.0	5. Japan	 83.0</p>
<p>malt shipment643.0	malt shipment 490.0</p>
<p>*preliminary.</p>
<p>Sources: CWB, Canadian Grain Commission.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Reuters Winnipeg Bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
